EmailTemplate.textOnly:
Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

Thank you for your interest in Arizona State University! We do not offer an undergraduate degree in physical therapy, but we have a BS in kinesiology, which is a good foundation to use to pursue a graduate program in physical therapy. Check out the details on this degree here: https://webapp4.asu.edu/programs/t5/majorinfo/ASU00/NUKINBS/undergrad/false

Another program that may interest you is the BS in exercise and wellness - find more information here: https://webapp4.asu.edu/programs/t5/majorinfo/ASU00/ECEXWBS/undergrad/false

I encourage you to view the Bureau of Labor and Statistics website (http://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/physical-therapists.htm), which can be very useful when looking into a particular career path. You can view relevant information on physical therapy qualifications, job outlook, earnings, etc. You may also want to check out the American Physical Therapy Association (http://www.apta.org/PTEducation/Overview/)

To receive guidance on declaring a major and what else you can do to prepare for a physical therapy program, I invite you to speak with an advisor in our pre-health department. You can reach an advisor at 480-965-2365 or online at the following site: http://prehealth.asu.edu/connect/advising

Sincerely,

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}

If you have any additional information or questions related to this, please reply to this email.

{!Case.Thread_Id}
